From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:21:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a killed standby's marker does not outlive it

A standby (gateway.runtime_lock_wait_seconds) removed gateway.standby only in a finally of the process that waited. When that process was SIGKILLed or OOM-killed while it waited, the file stayed in HERMES_HOME for good, since a gateway that boots with no predecessor never writes or removes it. A supervisor probe that skips the health check while a standby waits then passed on the file alone, so a hung gateway was never restarted.

The waiting standby now touches the marker every 2 seconds and writes its host name in it. A marker untouched for 10 seconds is stale: the listener relay ignores it, and the gateway that reserves the profile removes it. A fresh marker is a successor that waits for this gateway and stays. No new key.
